# `fj` CLI — Forgejo

Forgejo's CLI (`fj`) is installed via Homebrew as a standalone binary. It auto-detects the remote host from the git remote in the current directory.

See **[docs/fj-guide.md](../../docs/fj-guide.md)** for the full command reference (issues, PRs, conventions).

## Remote detection

`fj` reads the git remote URL from the current repo. Local Cove remotes use `https://git.cove.local/<owner>/<repo>.git`. The `cove-push` token in git's credential helper handles auth (set up by `cove up`).

SSH (`git@forgejo-localhost:...`) is also available as an optional transport — see `~/.agents/agents-md-detail/cove.md` for SSH config details.

## HTTPS auth

`cove up` caches a persistent API token (`cove-push`) in git's credential helper so `fj` can push over HTTPS without prompting.

## Issues

```bash
# Create an issue (title is the FIRST positional argument, NOT --title)
fj issue create "Title" --body-file <path>

# Comment on an issue
fj issue comment <ID> --body-file <path>

# List issues
fj issue list

# View an issue
fj issue view <ID>

# Close an issue
fj issue close <ID>
```

**Important:** `fj issue create` does **not** have a `--title` flag — the title is the first positional argument. Using `--title` will fail with a syntax error. Always use `--body-file` for body text (not `--body`).

## Draft / Ready status

Forgejo uses the PR title to determine draft status:

- **Draft:** title starts with `WIP:` (case-insensitive) — PR **cannot** be merged
- **Ready:** title does **not** start with `WIP:`

```bash
# Create a draft PR
fj pr create "WIP: my change"

# Mark ready (remove WIP: prefix)
fj pr edit <PR> title "my change"

# Mark draft (add WIP: prefix)
fj pr edit <PR> title "WIP: my change"
```

## Checking CI status

```bash
fj actions tasks
```

## The Core Pattern

```
fj pr view <ID> <action>
```

**All inspection actions are subcommands of `fj pr view`**, not of `fj pr`. The PR ID goes **before** the action. This is the inverse of `gh`, where actions are top-level subcommands of `gh pr`.

### Common Mistakes

```
WRONG: fj pr diff 12              # "diff" is not a subcommand of "fj pr"
RIGHT: fj pr view 12 diff         # "diff" is a subcommand of "fj pr view"

WRONG: fj pr view 13 --comments   # --comments is not a flag
RIGHT: fj pr view 13 comments     # "comments" is a positional subcommand

WRONG: fj pr comments 13          # "comments" is not a subcommand of "fj pr"
RIGHT: fj pr view 13 comments     # "comments" is under "fj pr view"
```

### `gh` → `fj` Mapping

If you know `gh`, use this translation table:

| `gh` command | `fj` equivalent |
|---|---|
| `gh pr diff 12` | `fj pr view 12 diff` |
| `gh pr view 12 --comments` | `fj pr view 12 comments` |
| `gh pr view 12 --files` | `fj pr view 12 files` |
| `gh pr view 12 --commits` | `fj pr view 12 commits` |
| `gh pr view 12 --labels` | `fj pr view 12 labels` |

### All `fj pr view` subcommands

```bash
# View the diff (base..head)
fj pr view <PR#> diff

# Get patch format (pipeable to git apply)
fj pr view <PR#> diff --patch
# or: fj pr view <PR#> diff -p

# Open the diff in $EDITOR
fj pr view <PR#> diff --editor

# List files changed (no diffs, just names)
fj pr view <PR#> files

# List commits on the PR branch
fj pr view <PR#> commits

# View all comments on a PR
fj pr view <PR#> comments

# View a specific comment by index (0-indexed)
fj pr view <PR#> comment <IDX>

# View the title and body
fj pr view <PR#> body

# View labels
fj pr view <PR#> labels
```

